cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "MatScout-4090: local high-throughput AI-for-materials discovery pipeline"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "MatScout-4090 contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/maruyamakoju/matscout-4090"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-05-23"
keywords:
  - materials discovery
  - machine-learning interatomic potentials
  - CHGNet
  - MACE
  - high-throughput screening
  - battery
  - solar
  - catalysis
  - CO2 capture
abstract: >-
  MatScout-4090 is a local pipeline for inorganic-materials discovery across battery,
  semiconductor, catalyst, solar, and CO2-capture applications. It generates candidate
  structures (substitution + prototype enumeration), relaxes them with a CHGNet/MACE
  ensemble, computes ML formation energies from elemental references, scores candidates
  with application-specific objectives plus novelty and synthesizability, ranks them
  (Pareto + weighted), and exports DFT-ready VASP/QE decks for cluster verification.
